<section>
    <h2 class="page-heading">CSS variables defined for the accordion component.</h2>

    <p>
        The following sections outline all of the css variables that can be set to alter the styling of the Accordion component.
        You can of course also override its style classes directly.
    </p>

    <section class="code-table">

        <h3 id="outline-misc-variables" class="code-table__heading">Accordion heading/accordion item panel outline/miscellaneous variables</h3>
        <p>
            There are focus indicators (outlines) applied using <span class="code-span">:focus-visible</span> for the Accordion heading
            and for the actual accordion item panels if it uses <span class="code-span">tabindex=0</span>
        </p>
        <table aria-labelledby="outline-misc-variables">

            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="col">Variable Name</th>
                    <th scope="col">Default Value</th>
                    <th scope="col">Description</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td>--br-comp-accordion-outline-style</td>
                    <td>var(--br-comp-all-outline-style)</td>
                    <td>The style of the outline - uses the shared component variable.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>--br-comp-accordion-outline-width</td>
                    <td>var(--br-comp-all-outline-width)</td>
                    <td>The outline width - uses the shared component variable.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>--br-comp-accordion-outline-offset</td>
                    <td>0px</td>
                    <td>The outline offset - <b>does not use the shared variable.</b></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>--br-comp-accordion-outline-colour</td>
                    <td>var(--br-comp-all-outline-colour)</td>
                    <td>The outline colour - uses the shared component variable.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>--br-comp-accordion-selected-hover</td>
                    <td>var(--br-comp-all-selection-colour)</td>
                    <td>The background colour on hover of a selected tab - uses the shared component variable.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>--br-comp-accordion-hover</td>
                    <td>var(--br-comp-all-link-hover-background-colour)</td>
                    <td>
                        The background colour on hover of an unselected accordion header - uses the shared component variable.
                        <strong>Note:</strong> According headings are buttons not links, but this existing css variable was suitable.
                    </td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </section>
    <section class="code-table">

